# Tests

Each test starts the app with a migrated database[[if eq .DB "sqlite"]] (in-memory SQLite)[[else]] (from `.env.testing`)[[end]],
and leaves no rows behind:

```go
func TestArticles(t *testing.T) {
	app := anetostest.New(t, setup)
	[[if .API]]app.Get("/api/v1/articles").AssertOK()[[else]]app.Get("/articles").AssertOK().AssertSee("Articles")[[end]]
}
```

- **Requests:** [[if .API]]`app.PostJSON(url, body)`, `.AssertStatus(201)`,
  `.AssertJSON(…)`[[else]]`app.PostForm(url, values)` (the CSRF token is sent for you),
  `.AssertRedirect(…)`, `.AssertSee(…)`[[end]]. A logged-in user:
  `anetostest.ActingAs(app, user)`.
- **Rows:** factories in `database/factories/`
  (`post := anetostest.Create(app, factories.Posts)`), and
  `anetostest.AssertDatabaseHas[models.Post](app, models.PostCols.Title.Eq("Hi"))`.
- **Fakes:** options of `anetostest.New`: `anetostest.FakeQueue()`
  (then `anetostest.AssertDispatched[jobs.X](app, func(j jobs.X) bool {…})`),
  `FakeEvents(…)`, `FakePubSub()`; mail is never sent in tests.
  `app.Freeze(t0)` and `app.Travel(d)` move the clock `anetos.Now(ctx)` reads.

Run one test: `go test -run TestArticles ./...`. Then
`go tool anetos check`. Docs: `go tool anetos docs guides/testing`.
